<title>CHINA: IBM invests $20 mln in Pudong company.</title>
<headline>IBM invests $20 mln in Pudong company.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>International Business Machines Corp (IBM) is investing $20 million in a wholly owned subsidiary in the Pudong New Area of Shanghai, a company spokewoman said on Friday.</p>
<p>The subsidiary, IBM Engineering and Technology (Shanghai) Co Ltd, in the Waigaoqiao bonded area of Pudong, is IBM's 13th operation in China, she said.</p>
<p>The subsidiary will be involved in storage and after-sales services when it starts operations early next year, she said without elaborating.</p>
</text>
